gamepad state in save states -- no upstream issue exists for it.
core/input_hw/gamepad.c holds the 6-button pad's TH level, pulse counter,
timeout and TH latency in file scope and state_save never wrote them, so
state_load's system_reset left a restored 6-button game on reset values
and it diverged within a few frames. STATE_VERSION stays as it is: the
loader compares that string, and older states are nobody's concern here.
--- a/core/input_hw/gamepad.c
+++ b/core/input_hw/gamepad.c
@@ -221,6 +221,26 @@
   gamepad[port].State = data;
 }
 
+int gamepad_context_save(uint8 *state)
+{
+  int bufferptr = 0;
+
+  save_param(gamepad, sizeof(gamepad));
+  save_param(flipflop, sizeof(flipflop));
+  save_param(&latch, sizeof(latch));
+  return bufferptr;
+}
+
+int gamepad_context_load(uint8 *state)
+{
+  int bufferptr = 0;
+
+  load_param(gamepad, sizeof(gamepad));
+  load_param(flipflop, sizeof(flipflop));
+  load_param(&latch, sizeof(latch));
+  return bufferptr;
+}
+
